# Connection strings for Prisma against Supabase.
#
# Copy to `.env` in this directory and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file
# is not, and must never gain a real password.
#
# Find both strings in the Supabase dashboard under Project Settings ->
# Database -> Connection string. The project ref is the subdomain of your
# project URL.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATABASE_URL - Supavisor transaction mode, port 6543
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What the application queries through.
#
# `pgbouncer=true` is NOT optional. Transaction mode does not support prepared
# statements, and Prisma without this flag produces intermittent
# `prepared statement "s0" already exists` failures. They appear only when
# concurrency exceeds the pool size, which means they appear during a live exam
# window and never once in testing.
#
# `connection_limit` is per worker process. Total workers x connection_limit
# must stay under the project's Pool Size or workers starve each other.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.PROJECT_REF:PASSWORD@aws-0-REGION.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true&connection_limit=1"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DIRECT_URL - session mode, port 5432
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What migrations run through. DDL needs a real session; a transaction-pooled
# connection cannot hold advisory locks across statements, which is how Prisma
# serialises concurrent deploys.
#
# Two forms. Prefer the first:
#
#   Session-mode pooler (below). IPv4 on every tier.
#
#   Direct: postgresql://postgres:PASSWORD@db.PROJECT_REF.supabase.co:5432/postgres
#   This is IPv6-only unless you have bought the IPv4 add-on. On a typical
#   IPv4-only CI runner or home connection it fails with ENETUNREACH, which
#   reads like a wrong password and is not one.
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://postgres.PROJECT_REF:PASSWORD@aws-0-REGION.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres"
